# Uploaded media and signed contracts must never be committed. Contracts in
# particular contain personal data + signatures; they belong in Cloudinary /
# object storage, not in version control.
backend/uploads/
backend/private_contracts/

# ...but DO track the env templates (no secrets in them) — the new host needs
# them as the canonical list of variables to configure.
!.env.example
!backend/.env.example
!frontend/.env.example
!backend/tests/.env.test.example
# Local Claude Code state: settings.local.json, launch.json, worktrees.
# Ignored as a whole, with named exceptions below.
#
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: git cannot re-include anything under
# a directory that is itself excluded, so the directory has to stay
# visible and its CONTENTS get excluded instead. Without this the
# negations below silently do nothing.
.claude/*

# Project skills that are part of the repo's knowledge, not one machine's
# setup. These encode incidents that already happened here, and a
# scheduled or cloud run works from a clean checkout — anything not
# committed does not exist for it. The audit skill was written, never
# committed, and an overnight run could not find it.
#
# Listed one by one, deliberately. The rest of .claude/skills/ is
# general-purpose tooling that belongs to the machine rather than to this
# codebase, and a blanket `!.claude/skills/**` would sweep it in along
# with whatever anyone installs next.
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/site-audit/
!.claude/skills/visual-diff/
!.claude/skills/myisraelrental-frontend/

screenshots/

# Throwaway verification scripts. Written to drive a browser or probe the
# dev database while checking a change, then deleted. Ignored rather than
# committed so a stray one cannot be mistaken for tooling — the real
# checkers (screenshot.mjs, check-tile-contrast.mjs) have proper names.
scripts/.tmp-*
